# LINE ENDINGS ARE PART OF THE ARTIFACT CONTRACT (Oct 17).
#
# core.autocrlf=true is set on this machine and there was no attributes
# file, so git smudged pool/templates/index.html to CRLF on checkout while
# the committed review bundle stayed LF. The two committed blobs are
# byte-identical (112678 bytes, 1693 LF, 0 CRLF) — but the drive compares
# WORKING-TREE bytes, so test_bundle_parity check 2 went red on a tree whose
# commit was already at parity, and the deterministic zip could never match
# a rebuild from the smudged copy. These pins make the checked-out bytes
# equal the committed bytes, so parity is a property of the repository and
# not of how the tree happened to be checked out.
pool/templates/*.html text eol=lf
pool/static/*.js      text eol=lf
pool/static/*.css     text eol=lf

# The review README is a bundle INPUT too (make_bundle copies it in and dates
# it), so it is held to the same contract as the templates and statics: LF on
# every checkout, otherwise the zip it lands in cannot be reproduced.
installer/site_review_readme.txt text eol=lf

# The static image assets are binary, and the review bundle's parity check
# compares them byte for byte: never convert one.
pool/static/img/*.png -text

# The review bundle is a byte-for-byte artifact (templates, statics, README,
# the deterministic zip and its sha256 sidecar): never convert a byte of it.
dist_site_review/** -text

# ...except the sidecar, which is a POSIX checksum file: `sha256sum -c`
# rejects a line ending in CR, so this one stays LF everywhere.
dist_site_review/**/*.sha256 text eol=lf
